1. Project Overview

Multi-Modal RAG is a full-stack application that allows users to upload documents and ask questions about their content using a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) pipeline.

The backend processes documents, stores retrievable information in ChromaDB, and uses Google's Gemini model to generate responses. The frontend provides the chat interface and communicates with the backend API.

Main features
Upload supported documents, including PDFs.
Extract document content for processing.
Retrieve relevant information from stored document data.
Generate answers using Google Gemini.
Provide a browser-based chat interface.
Run the backend and frontend locally.
Deploy the backend and frontend independently.
Monitor backend availability using UptimeRobot.

Important: Image and diagram understanding depends on the multimodal extraction and retrieval functionality implemented in the application. It should be tested separately before claiming that all image-based document scenarios are supported.

