8. Frontend Environment Configuration

The frontend uses the environment variable:

NEXT_PUBLIC_PYTHON_API_URL

For local development, configure it in the appropriate frontend environment file if required by the source code.

For the deployed frontend, set it in the Render Static Site's environment settings.

Production value:

env
NEXT_PUBLIC_PYTHON_API_URL=https://multi-modal-rag-lyr4.onrender.com


Do not append /api unless the frontend source explicitly expects it. The existing configuration discussed during deployment uses the backend base URL.

Because Next.js embeds NEXT_PUBLIC_ variables into client-side bundles during the build, configure the variable before deploying or rebuilding the frontend.

If you change this value, trigger a new frontend deployment.

Important: This variable is public by design. Never put private API keys or other secrets in NEXT_PUBLIC_ variables.

